 Fix: read init.defaultBranch, or say \\\"assumed main\\\" in the summary. Also, three sequential 0.8 s git calls can exceed the 1.0 s soft per-check budget, which has no override. That costs only an annotation.\\n- P2-2 — _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py:25-26. Each part opens with a module docstring, and running the compiled part stores it into the namespace's __doc__. So ceo_boot.__doc__ becomes \\\"Extracted ceo-boot declarations executed by the facade.\\\" Fix: drop the part docstrings, or save and restore __doc__ around the loop.\\n- P2-3 — ceo-boot logic moved from .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py, which is not a canonical path, to .claude/hooks/_lib/**/*.py, which is canonical (canonical_edit/guards.py:34). Editing ceo-boot checks in an install now needs a sentinel. That tightens governance, but the CHANGELOG does not declare it for ceo-boot.\\n- P2-4 — .claude/commands/ceo-boot.md:35 still says \\\"the 24 Tier-S checks\\\"; everything else says 25, and the registry asserts 25.\\n- P2-5 (carried, not new) — check_hook_live_smoke (harness_governance.py) runs py_compile on every registered hook at each boot, which writes __pycache__/*.pyc next to the adopter's hooks.\",\"decision\":\"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS\",\"sentence\":\"No declared condition is false against this payload and no P0 was found, but two undeclared P1s must go to the signed annex: after the PLAN-197 split, sentinel-pattern derivation always falls back because it reads a file that no longer holds _PATTERNS, and the facade's never-dispatched spec-drift copy leaves the vacuity lint and its regression tests checking code that /ceo-boot does not run.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"PAYLOAD 6/32: nine new files under .claude/hooks/_lib/_ceo_boot_parts/ (the ceo-boot split, PLAN-197). I also read, from the redacted tree: the facade .claude/scripts/ceo-boot.py (its diff is in another payload), the loader _ceo_boot_parts/__init__.py, how install and upgrade enumerate files, and every module the parts load at runtim